    "15": {
      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "I am seated in the heart of everyone; from Me arise memory, knowledge, and their removal. I alone am to be known through all the Vedas; I am the author of Vedānta and indeed the knower of the Veda. Śrīdhara explains memory as arising from past experience, knowledge from contact between senses and their objects, and “removal” as the loss of either.",
